# VTID-03945 — commands run during this change

## Investigation
Read the post-VTID-03943 state of both routes on origin/main to confirm
the duplication this refactor removes was real, not assumed:
$ git show origin/main:services/gateway/src/routes/discover-search.ts | sed -n '305,357p'
  (18-line manual let-hiddenBreakdown-with-conditional-reassignment block)
$ git show origin/main:services/gateway/src/routes/discover-feed.ts | sed -n '190,249p'
  (5-line inline spread with its own geo-summing formula)

Confirmed the two formulas are NOT byte-identical in shape (search seeds
past_purchases:0 upfront and carries it forward across a conditional;
feed spreads hidden_breakdown directly into the response) even though
they compute the same underlying invariant (geo = pre-filter geo count +
limitations' own geo count) — exactly the kind of two-copies-of-one-rule
shape this repo's CHANGE LOG already names as a recurring defect source
(VTID-03644, VTID-03696, VTID-03943).

## Fix
services/gateway/src/services/limitations-filter.ts:
  1. Added LimitationsHiddenBreakdown (8 fields, matches
     applyUserLimitations()'s existing hidden_breakdown shape) and
     HiddenBreakdown (extends it with past_purchases) exported interfaces.
  2. LimitationsFilterResult now references LimitationsHiddenBreakdown
     instead of an inline duplicate object-type literal.
  3. Added buildHiddenBreakdown({preFilterGeoHidden, limitations,
     pastPurchasesHidden}) -> HiddenBreakdown — pure, no I/O.

services/gateway/src/routes/discover-search.ts:
  Replaced the 18-line manual hiddenBreakdown assembly (seed literal +
  conditional reassignment + final past-purchases spread) with:
    let limitationsBreakdown: LimitationsHiddenBreakdown | undefined;
    if (ctx) { ...; limitationsBreakdown = result.hidden_breakdown; }
    const hiddenBreakdown = buildHiddenBreakdown({
      preFilterGeoHidden: fetched.length - geoAllowed.length,
      limitations: limitationsBreakdown,
      pastPurchasesHidden: past_purchases_hidden,
    });

services/gateway/src/routes/discover-feed.ts:
  Replaced the inline response-object spread with:
    hidden_breakdown: buildHiddenBreakdown({
      preFilterGeoHidden: candidates.length - geoAllowed.length,
      limitations: hidden_breakdown,
      pastPurchasesHidden: past_purchases_hidden,
    }),

## New tests (extended the existing VTID-03943 test file)
services/gateway/test/limitations-filter.test.ts — added 7 tests for
buildHiddenBreakdown(): geo summing, category pass-through, past-purchases
pass-through, undefined-limitations (anonymous request) case, fully-empty
case, and two formula-equivalence tests that reproduce each route's exact
PRE-REFACTOR inline formula and assert buildHiddenBreakdown() returns the
byte-identical object — the concrete proof this refactor changes no
observable behavior in either route.

